#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:3
msgid "Security Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:5
msgid ""
"We take security seriously. CodeIgniter incorporates a number of features"
" and techniques to either enforce good security practices, or to enable "
"you to do so easily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:9
msgid ""
"We respect the `Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) "
"<https://owasp.org>`_ and follow their recommendations as much as "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:12
msgid ""
"The following comes from `OWASP Top Ten <https://owasp.org/www-project-"
"top-ten/>`_ and `OWASP API Security Top 10 <https://owasp.org/API-"
"Security/editions/2023/en/0x11-t10/>`_ identifying the top "
"vulnerabilities for web applications and apis. For each, we provide a "
"brief description, the OWASP recommendations, and then the CodeIgniter "
"provisions to address the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:25
msgid "OWASP Top 10 2021"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:28
msgid "A01:2021 Broken Access Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:30
msgid ""
"Access control enforces policy such that users cannot act outside of "
"their intended permissions. Failures typically lead to unauthorized "
"information disclosure, modification, or destruction of all data or "
"performing a business function outside the user's limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:35
msgid "Common access control vulnerabilities include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:37
msgid ""
"Violation of the principle of least privilege or deny by default, where "
"access should only be granted for particular capabilities, roles, or "
"users, but is available to anyone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:40
msgid ""
"Bypassing access control checks by modifying the URL (parameter tampering"
" or force browsing), internal application state, or the HTML page, or by "
"using an attack tool modifying API requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:43
msgid ""
"Permitting viewing or editing someone else's account, by providing its "
"unique identifier (insecure direct object references)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:45
msgid "Accessing API with missing access controls for POST, PUT and DELETE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:46
msgid ""
"Elevation of privilege. Acting as a user without being logged in or "
"acting as an admin when logged in as a user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:48
msgid ""
"Metadata manipulation, such as replaying or tampering with a JSON Web "
"Token (JWT) access control token, or a cookie or hidden field manipulated"
" to elevate privileges or abusing JWT invalidation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:51
msgid ""
"CORS misconfiguration allows API access from unauthorized/untrusted "
"origins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:52
msgid ""
"Force browsing to authenticated pages as an unauthenticated user or to "
"privileged pages as a standard user."
msgstr ""

