#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:58
msgid ""
"Access control is only effective in trusted server-side code or server-"
"less API, where the attacker cannot modify the access control check or "
"metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:61
msgid "Except for public resources, deny by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:62
msgid ""
"Implement access control mechanisms once and re-use them throughout the "
"application, including minimizing Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) "
"usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:64
msgid ""
"Model access controls should enforce record ownership rather than "
"accepting that the user can create, read, update, or delete any record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:66
msgid ""
"Unique application business limit requirements should be enforced by "
"domain models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:67
msgid ""
"Disable web server directory listing and ensure file metadata (e.g., "
".git) and backup files are not present within web roots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:69
msgid ""
"Log access control failures, alert admins when appropriate (e.g., "
"repeated failures)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:70
msgid ""
"Rate limit API and controller access to minimize the harm from automated "
"attack tooling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:72
msgid ""
"Stateful session identifiers should be invalidated on the server after "
"logout. Stateless JWT tokens should rather be short-lived so that the "
"window of opportunity for an attacker is minimized. For longer lived JWTs"
" it's highly recommended to follow the OAuth standards to revoke access."
msgstr ""

