#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:239
msgid "A04:2021 Insecure Design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:241
msgid ""
"Insecure design is a broad category representing different weaknesses, "
"expressed as “missing or ineffective control design.” Insecure design is "
"not the source for all other Top 10 risk categories. There is a "
"difference between insecure design and insecure implementation. We "
"differentiate between design flaws and implementation defects for a "
"reason, they have different root causes and remediation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:247
msgid ""
"A secure design can still have implementation defects leading to "
"vulnerabilities that may be exploited. An insecure design cannot be fixed"
" by a perfect implementation as by definition, needed security controls "
"were never created to defend against specific attacks. One of the factors"
" that contribute to insecure design is the lack of business risk "
"profiling inherent in the software or system being developed, and thus "
"the failure to determine what level of security design is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:257
msgid ""
"Establish and use a secure development lifecycle with AppSec "
"professionals to help evaluate and design security and privacy-related "
"controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:259
msgid ""
"Establish and use a library of secure design patterns or paved road ready"
" to use components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:261
msgid ""
"Use threat modeling for critical authentication, access control, business"
" logic, and key flows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:263
msgid "Integrate security language and controls into user stories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:264
msgid ""
"Integrate plausibility checks at each tier of your application (from "
"frontend to backend)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:266
msgid ""
"Write unit and integration tests to validate that all critical flows are "
"resistant to the threat model. Compile use-cases and misuse-cases for "
"each tier of your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:269
msgid ""
"Segregate tier layers on the system and network layers depending on the "
"exposure and protection needs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:271
msgid "Segregate tenants robustly by design throughout all tiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concepts/security.rst:272
msgid "Limit resource consumption by user or service"
msgstr ""

